## Today's Recall Highlights

A staggering **11 recalls** from Spring & Mulberry Inc. have brought them to the forefront of today's shelf check. This brand, already in our "F"-grade list for historical recall frequency, continues to underwhelm with quality control. Products recalled today include their Mango Chili Date-Sweetened Chocolate and Mulberry Fennel Date-Sweetened Chocolate, both due to potential Salmonella contamination. Given the severity of Class I recalls, these products posed a direct and imminent danger to consumer health. 

## Brands Under Scrutiny

Spring & Mulberry tops the list, yet again, as a heavily scrutinized brand. With 11 recalls this year, exclusively in the Class I category, their track record demands immediate attention. Their recall performance this year alone would be concerning, but paired with repeated instances of the same violations, it paints a concerning picture. 

## Larger Trends

Today marks the 759th recall this year, and we're only halfway through the calendar. The monthly breakdown suggests this is not slowing down, with 213 recalls happening just last month. Repeat offenders like Spring & Mulberry and Moonlight Packing Corporation are a systemic issue that warrants deeper investigation into their operational practices.

## What Can We Do?

Stay informed. As consumers, understanding which brands consistently fall short is the first line of defense. Avoid brands with repetitive incidents and hold them accountable through feedback and informed purchasing choices. Regulators can only do so much; it's the collective effort of consumers that can catalyze change.
